---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import TimeLineElement from "../components/cv/TimeLine.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Resume" sideBarActiveItemID="cv">
  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Profile</div>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-10 text-justify">
    Engineering Physics graduate specializing in control systems, electronics, and industrial IoT. 
    Experienced designing and deploying control algorithms (MPC, LQR, PID, RL) and vision-based localization.
    Trained in firmware, PCB design, and FPGA through the Korea Chamber of Commerce and Industry (KCCI) program.
    Creator and co-creator of 3 published academic papers.
  </div>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Education</div>
  </div>

  <div class="time-line-container grid gap-4 mb-10">
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Bachelor of Engineering, Engineering Physics (Instrumentation and Control)"
      subtitle="August 2022 to August 2026 at Institut Teknologi Bandung (ITB), Bandung, Indonesia. GPA 3.68 / 4.00"
    >
      Undergraduate thesis on an autonomous vehicle that detects and avoids road damage, combining YOLO-based perception
      with a Deep Q-Network planner in the CARLA simulator.
    </TimeLineElement>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Experience</div>
  </div>

  <div class="time-line-container mb-10">
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Research Assistant at Directorate of Research and Innovation, ITB"
      subtitle="From December 2025 to July 2026 at Bandung, Indonesia"
    >
      Investigated how autonomous vehicles can steer around potholes while keeping the ride smooth. Collected and
      annotated the road damage dataset, built the detection model, and designed the motion planning algorithm. The work
      was supported by ITB and National Taiwan University of Science and Technology (NTUST).
    </TimeLineElement>
    <TimeLineElement
      title="System Engineer (Intern) at PT. AVS Simulator"
      subtitle="From July 2025 to August 2025"
    >
      Created a replica of a MOZA R12 steering system on an STM32 microcontroller to be used in a truck driving
      simulator.
    </TimeLineElement>
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Embedded Engineer (Intern) at PT. Cultination"
      subtitle="From June 2024 to August 2024"
    >
      Built an automated monitoring system for fish ponds, with sensors and ESP32 firmware feeding live readings to a
      smartphone app, so that farm staff can keep watch remotely.
    </TimeLineElement>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Leadership</div>
  </div>

  <div class="time-line-container mb-10">
    <TimeLineElement title="Vice Director, Mechanical Division at University Robotics Unit" subtitle="">
      Co-led a five-person team that developed two humanoid robots from start to finish. To save budget, the team built
      its own Anet A8 3D printer from parts, then used it to enlarge the robots' chest structure for a bigger controller
      compartment and to print replacements whenever parts broke.
    </TimeLineElement>
    <TimeLineElement title="Team Leader, Bridge Monitoring System" subtitle="">
      Led a three-person team in delivering a bridge monitoring system, taking it from client requirements through to a
      working prototype.
    </TimeLineElement>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Honors &amp; Achievements</div>
  </div>

  <ul class="list-disc mx-6 mb-10 grid gap-2">
    <li>
      <b>Best Indonesian Student Paper Award</b>, 15th Asian Control Conference (ASCC) 2026, June 2026. Recognition for
      the research on pothole-aware motion planning for autonomous vehicles.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Certifications &amp; Training</div>
  </div>

  <ul class="list-disc mx-6 mb-10 grid gap-2">
    <li>Certified SOLIDWORKS Associate (CSWA), Dassault Systemes, December 2024</li>
    <li>
      Basics of Mitsubishi PLC (20 hours), Instrumentation, Control, and Automation Research Group, ITB, November 2025.
      GX Works2, GX Works3, and GT Designer 3.
    </li>
    <li>
      Overseas Technical Expert Training (500 hours), Korea Chamber of Commerce &amp; Industry (KCCI), July 2026 to
      November 2026. 200 hours of Korean language and culture, plus 300 hours of vocational training in firmware
      development, electronic hardware design, and semiconductor design.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Skills</div>
  </div>

  <ul class="list-disc mx-6 grid gap-2">
    <li><b>AI &amp; Computer Vision:</b> Python, TensorFlow, PyTorch, OpenCV, YOLO, Deep Reinforcement Learning (DQN), CARLA</li>
    <li><b>Industrial Automation &amp; IIoT:</b> Mitsubishi and Omron PLCs, Weintek HMI, MQTT, Node-RED, PostgreSQL</li>
    <li><b>Embedded Systems:</b> C++, C#, STM32, ESP32</li>
    <li><b>Robotics:</b> Introductory ROS / ROS2</li>
    <li><b>CAD:</b> SOLIDWORKS (CSWA certified)</li>
    <li><b>Languages:</b> English (advanced), Korean (beginner, currently studying)</li>
  </ul>
</BaseLayout>
